# Input
```js
/* should generate diagnostics */
const foo = bar
export { foo }
Object()
export { baz } from 'bar'
Object()
export * as qux from 'bar'
Object()
import quux from 'bar'
Object()
export default Object()

```

# Diagnostics
```
invalidModule.js:4:1 lint/nursery/noObjectConstructor  FIXABLE  ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  i Calling Object without arguments creates an empty object.
  
    2 │ const foo = bar
    3 │ export { foo }
  > 4 │ Object()
      │ ^^^^^^^^
    5 │ export { baz } from 'bar'
    6 │ Object()
  
  i Writing {} is shorter, and it always creates a plain object, even if other code replaces the global Object.
  
  i This rule belongs to the nursery group, which means it is not yet stable and may change in the future. Visit https://biomejs.dev/linter/#nursery for more information.
  
  i Safe fix: Use an object literal.
  
     2  2 │   const foo = bar
     3  3 │   export { foo }
     4    │ - Object()
        4 │ + ({})
     5  5 │   export { baz } from 'bar'
     6  6 │   Object()
  

```

